From 3d95aa2fb2605f85fe5f6a8a0ddac6cebb864e50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TekRantGaming <craigferels896@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 06:24:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] D3D12: resolve readback reads the bytes written, and reaches
 the game sooner

With resolution scaling, the readback copied from the start of the
destination texture instead of the bytes the resolve wrote. Games that
resolve into part of a texture got the wrong data: Trials Evolution's
texture page requests came back nearly empty (about 350 different values
instead of 23000) and its occlusion depth map never arrived, so texture
pages were not streamed and objects were culled against an old map.
Vulkan already read the written range.

readback_resolve fast also handed the game the previous resolve of each
buffer, two frames old for buffers it alternates between. Each copy now
goes into guest memory as soon as its submission completes (checked on
draws, copies, swaps and while waiting for commands), the submission is
started right after the copy, and a buffer is only read once the GPU has
finished writing it. readback_resolve_early (on) switches this.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
